From 83a8958febb95a00c142dfa3e1591f2b1161a395 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ggbdpq <ggbdpq@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 00:34:49 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] gateway: the CR a glm-5.3-flash* replica stitches into
 tool-call arguments

Yetone's review of the two earlier rounds (#4256): the cure changed
healthy replies and cost the relay hot path. This one keeps to the routes
the defect was seen on, and holds a cut escape the way the encoders do:

- The cure runs only on glm-5.3-flash* routes (glmFlash, the way
  grokModel scopes its rule): a relay installs crTidy for those models
  alone, translate sets Request.CR the way it sets Request.Grok, and the
  encoder wrapper crEncoder and the whole-reply pass crResult hang off
  that flag. Another model's reply goes as it came, healthy or not.
- The relay's mends wait per call (crTidy.calls, by Chat's tool_calls
  index, Messages' block index, Responses' item id), so a \r\n cut
  across two fragments arrives as the pair it is; a \r the next
  fragment does not answer with \n is the defect, and goes. A line's
  end is looked for in the new bytes of a read alone, and a region
  without the escape is said from where it lies: a 24MB line in 32KB
  reads costs a scan (23ms here; the round-2 way took 2.45s).
- The events whose delta is an argument are read from the event's own
  type or shape: a text delta that only mentions the arguments' event
  names stands, \r and all.
- A custom tool's raw input (Codex's apply_patch) is read as bytes: the
  CRLF pair is the line ending it says, a lone CR goes.
- The encoders' dropper is said at a call's end: a lone \r goes, a bare
  \ is said as it came (crEncoder.say).

Fixes #4256

Run: go test -tags nogui ./internal/gateway/... (ok). The healthy
split-CRLF relays of all three protocols, the custom input's, the text
delta's and the scope's tests fail on the round-2 branch and pass here;
unwiring the flag reds the cure tests again.

Generated-by: GLM-5.3-Flash (ZCode)
